From 01f9eb2e7557c7783c3635748a68b3d1ac4075d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:55:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] WIP: port core registries, config, knives, and JSON
 data formats to NeoForge 1.21.1

- Port DelightfulItems (already done prior), DelightfulBlocks, DelightfulFluids, DFluidType,
  Util, Modid, Mods, DelightfulConfig, Delightful.java, CommonProxy/ClientProxy to the
  DeferredHolder/ModConfigSpec/NeoForge event bus APIs.
- Delete Botania, Aether Redux, Deep Aether, Let Fish Love, DPacketHandler, JEI, and
  AppleSkin compat (real 3rd-party APIs, not supported in target pack). Strip the
  matching branches in Knives.java / TerraKnifeItem / AlfKnifeItem / ElementiumKnifeItem /
  AlfsteelTier so they compile and register as plain steel-tier fallbacks (Alf remains
  Mythic-Botany-gated via its own getModid()).
- Redesign knife attribute-modifier hooks (DKnifeItem, Pearlescent/Zanite/Valkyrum knives)
  around the 1.21 data-component ItemAttributeModifiers API, since the old per-slot
  Multimap<Attribute,AttributeModifier> override is gone.
- Replace the pie-edibility mixins (Item#isEdible/getFoodProperties no longer exist) with a
  single PieEdibilityMixin against IItemExtension#getFoodProperties(ItemStack,LivingEntity).
  Replace the AbstractFurnaceBlockEntity#dataAccess access transformer with a Mixin
  @Accessor (FurnaceDataAccessorAccessor) instead of guessing SRG names.
- Drop the Chicken.FOOD_ITEMS/Parrot.TAME_FOOD access-transformer hack entirely: those fields
  no longer exist in 1.21, replaced by vanilla ItemTags.CHICKEN_FOOD/PARROT_FOOD (to be wired
  in datagen).
- Bulk-migrate resource data: rename forge: condition-codec ids to neoforge: (item_exists,
  mod_loaded, not, and, or, tag_empty, true, false) and restructure all 705
  {"type":"forge:conditional","recipes":[...]} wrapper recipes into the new embedded
  "neoforge:conditions" format (splitting multi-variant files into _altN siblings). Convert
  the 9 "forge:nbt" water-bottle ingredient matches to neoforge:components
  (DataComponentIngredient) since ItemStack NBT ingredient matching is gone. Move
  data/forge/loot_modifiers -> data/neoforge/loot_modifiers and
  data/delightful/forge/biome_modifier -> data/delightful/neoforge/biome_modifier to match
  NeoForge's renamed built-in registry namespace.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
